# @khalid64927/* packages (qr-studio-sg-payload, qr-studio-sg-qr) live on GitHub
# Packages, which — unlike npmjs.org — requires authentication for every install, even
# of a public repository's packages. npm interpolates ${NPM_TOKEN} from the environment
# at install time, so no secret lives in this file: set NPM_TOKEN to a GitHub PAT with
# read:packages, locally in your shell env and in Vercel's project environment
# variables. See the root README's Publishing section for how to get one.
@khalid64927:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
